## 4. Koala (pair) — loc_treehouse, loc_tallest_tree, loc_blossom_tree (level_2)

animal-koala = Koala
animal-koala-more = More about the koala

# Facts (never a place word, ANIM-007); kiga: one word next to a picture
mission-koala-facts-kiga = pouch
mission-koala-facts-klasse1 = I sleep a lot. I live in Australia. Babies live in a pouch.
mission-koala-facts-klasse2 = Koalas live in Australia. They sleep up to twenty hours a day. A koala baby spends its first months in its mother's pouch. Koalas eat almost nothing but eucalyptus.
mission-koala-facts-klasse3 = Koalas come from Australia and look like little teddy bears, but they are not bears. They eat almost nothing but eucalyptus. These leaves give them little energy, so koalas sleep up to twenty hours a day. A koala baby is called a joey and lives in its mother's pouch for its first months. Later it rides on her back.

# loc_treehouse — wooden tree house with a rope ladder in an old oak
mission-koala-riddle-loc_treehouse-kiga = treehouse
mission-koala-riddle-loc_treehouse-klasse1 = We like to climb. A house is up high. A rope ladder hangs down.
mission-koala-riddle-loc_treehouse-klasse2 = The koalas sit high up in a little wooden house with a roof and a window. The only way up is a rope ladder.
mission-koala-riddle-loc_treehouse-klasse3 = Koalas love to climb, and they like it best high up. Our two koalas have found a little wooden house that sits between thick branches. It has a roof, a window and a rope ladder. Up there they feel as cosy as in a nest.

# loc_tallest_tree — the tallest tree of the zoo, koalas at the very top
mission-koala-riddle-loc_tallest_tree-kiga = treetop
mission-koala-riddle-loc_tallest_tree-klasse1 = We sit at the top. Nothing here is higher. We can see everything!
mission-koala-riddle-loc_tallest_tree-klasse2 = The koalas sit at the very top of the tallest tree in the zoo. It is twice as tall as all the other trees.
mission-koala-riddle-loc_tallest_tree-klasse3 = From the very top you can see the farthest, and koalas know that too. Our two koalas have picked the tallest tree in the whole zoo. Its trunk is so thick that three children cannot hug it. Its crown towers far above all the other trees.

# loc_blossom_tree — tree full of pink blossoms, petals drifting down, bees
mission-koala-riddle-loc_blossom_tree-kiga = blossoms
mission-koala-riddle-loc_blossom_tree-klasse1 = We like pretty colours. Everything is pink. It smells sweet.
mission-koala-riddle-loc_blossom_tree-klasse2 = The koalas sit in a tree that is all pink. Little pink flakes float softly to the ground, and bees hum.
mission-koala-riddle-loc_blossom_tree-klasse3 = In spring one tree in the zoo puts on a pink dress. The koalas think it is beautiful and have climbed up. When the wind blows, little pink petals drift down like snow. Busy bees hum around the branches.

# shown when the animal is back in its enclosure (mission complete, GAME-RESCUE §8)
mission-koala-home = Great! The koalas are home again.

## 5. Elephant — loc_fountain, loc_log_pile, loc_big_ball (level_2)

animal-elephant = Elephant
animal-elephant-more = More about the elephant

# Facts (never a place word, ANIM-007); kiga: one word next to a picture
mission-elephant-facts-kiga = trunk
mission-elephant-facts-klasse1 = I have a trunk. I am very heavy. My ears are huge.
mission-elephant-facts-klasse2 = Elephants are the biggest animals on land. With their trunk they can smell, drink and grab things. They fan themselves cool air with their big ears.
mission-elephant-facts-klasse3 = Elephants are the biggest animals that live on land. Their trunk is a nose and a hand at the same time: with it they smell, drink and even pick up small branches. Every day an elephant eats as much hay and grass as fits into a whole cart. Elephants never forget who was kind to them. An elephant family sticks together.

# loc_fountain — round stone fountain with a water jet and coins
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_fountain-kiga = fountain
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_fountain-klasse1 = I am thirsty. The water jumps up high. Coins shine at the bottom.
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_fountain-klasse2 = The elephant drinks where water sprays into the air from the middle of a round stone basin. Coins shine on the bottom of the basin.
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_fountain-klasse3 = The elephant is very thirsty and has a good nose for water. It has found a round stone basin. In the middle, water shoots high into the air and splashes back down. Shiny coins lie on the bottom, because visitors make a wish here. Now it sucks up water with its trunk and gives itself a shower.

# loc_log_pile — stacked logs of the fallen tree, sawdust
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_log_pile-kiga = log pile
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_log_pile-klasse1 = I am very strong. I carry heavy wood. It smells of sawdust.
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_log_pile-klasse2 = The elephant stands by thick tree trunks stacked neatly on top of each other. Sawdust lies all around in the grass.
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_log_pile-klasse3 = After the storm the zookeepers sawed the fallen tree into thick pieces and stacked them up neatly. The elephant loves that! At home it likes to roll heavy tree trunks around. Now it stands next to the wood, and all around it smells of fresh sawdust.

# loc_big_ball — giant red-and-white play ball on the lawn
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_big_ball-kiga = ball
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_big_ball-klasse1 = I like to play. It is round and red. It is bigger than you!
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_big_ball-klasse2 = The elephant plays with something huge and round, red and white. It pushes it across the grass with its trunk.
mission-elephant-riddle-loc_big_ball-klasse3 = Elephants are clever and like to play, even when they are grown up. So the zookeepers gave them a toy that is bigger than a child. It is round, red and white, and it rolls when you push it. Our elephant nudges it with its trunk and trumpets with joy.

# shown when the animal is back in its enclosure (mission complete, GAME-RESCUE §8)
mission-elephant-home = Great! The elephant is home again.

## 6. Goldfish — loc_waterfall, loc_water_wheel, loc_willow (level_3)

animal-goldfish = Goldfish
animal-goldfish-more = More about the goldfish

# Facts (never a place word, ANIM-007); kiga: one word next to a picture
mission-goldfish-facts-kiga = fins
mission-goldfish-facts-klasse1 = I am orange. I have fins. I breathe in water.
mission-goldfish-facts-klasse2 = Goldfish originally come from China. They breathe under water with gills. They steer with their fins as if with little oars.
mission-goldfish-facts-klasse3 = Goldfish come from China, where people bred them a very long time ago. They do not breathe with lungs but with gills. They steer and brake with their fins as if with little oars. A goldfish can live for many years, sometimes longer than you have been alive. It even recognises the person who feeds it.

# loc_waterfall — waterfall from a rock ledge into the stream, white foam
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_waterfall-kiga = waterfall
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_waterfall-klasse1 = I like to swim. It is loud here. White foam!
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_waterfall-klasse2 = The goldfish swims where the water tumbles down from high stones and foams white.
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_waterfall-klasse3 = The little goldfish has swum far upstream, almost to the edge of the zoo. There the water falls down over a rocky ledge and splashes in every direction. It roars so loudly that you can hardly hear yourself. Something orange flashes in the white foam.

# loc_water_wheel — wooden water wheel turning in the stream at a tiny mill hut
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_water_wheel-kiga = waterwheel
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_water_wheel-klasse1 = Clatter, clatter! A wheel turns round. It is made of wood.
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_water_wheel-klasse2 = The goldfish swims next to a big wooden wheel that turns in the water and clatters loudly. A little hut stands beside it.
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_water_wheel-klasse3 = A tiny wooden mill stands on the bank. The water pushes a big wheel that keeps on turning. Clatter, clatter, it goes, and glittering drops fall down. The goldfish thinks this is fun and swims in circles right beside it.

# loc_willow — weeping willow whose branches hang into the stream
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_willow-kiga = willow
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_willow-klasse1 = I like it quiet. Long branches hang down. They touch the water.
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_willow-klasse2 = The goldfish hides where a tree lets its long, thin branches hang down into the water.
mission-goldfish-riddle-loc_willow-klasse3 = On the bank stands a tree that looks as if it were sadly hanging its head. Its long, thin branches fall like a green curtain into the water. Underneath it is shady and calm. That is exactly where the goldfish is hiding.

# Fish bowl (GAME-RESCUE "goldfish bowl"): feedback bubbles and the hint on the info board
mission-goldfish-needs-bowl = I need a bowl of water!
mission-goldfish-bowl-empty = There is no water in the bowl!
mission-goldfish-bowl-filled = The bowl is full of water.
mission-goldfish-in-bowl = Splash! The goldfish is in the bowl.
mission-goldfish-bowl-hint-kiga = bowl
mission-goldfish-bowl-hint-klasse1 = I need a bowl. The bowl needs water.
mission-goldfish-bowl-hint-klasse2 = Bring a big bowl full of water. Only in it can the goldfish travel home.
mission-goldfish-bowl-hint-klasse3 = A goldfish cannot walk along the path. You need a big glass bowl, and the zookeepers keep one in their house. Fill it with water, and the goldfish can jump in.

# shown when the animal is back in its enclosure (mission complete, GAME-RESCUE §8)
mission-goldfish-home = Great! The goldfish is home again.

## 7. Monkey — loc_pirate_ship, loc_carousel, loc_trampoline (level_3)

animal-monkey = Monkey
animal-monkey-more = More about the monkey

# Facts (never a place word, ANIM-007); kiga: one word next to a picture
mission-monkey-facts-kiga = tail
mission-monkey-facts-klasse1 = I climb very well. I like bananas. I am cheeky.
mission-monkey-facts-klasse2 = Monkeys are very good climbers. They can grab things with their hands, just like you. They are curious and love to play tricks.
mission-monkey-facts-klasse3 = Monkeys are true climbing artists and swing from branch to branch. Their hands look almost like yours, and they can even peel fruit with them. Many monkeys hold on with their tail like a third hand. They are very curious and learn quickly. They like best to live together with their family.

# loc_pirate_ship — pirate ship climbing frame: mast, sail, black flag, treasure chest
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_pirate_ship-kiga = ship
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_pirate_ship-klasse1 = Ahoy! I am a pirate now. I sit on the mast.
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_pirate_ship-klasse2 = The monkey is playing pirate now. It sits at the top of the mast and looks for treasure.
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_pirate_ship-klasse3 = The cheeky monkey has found a new home – or so it thinks. It has a big sail, a black flag and a treasure chest. It shouts "Ahoy!" and climbs all the way up.

# loc_carousel — small carousel with wooden horses and a striped roof
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_carousel-kiga = carousel
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_carousel-klasse1 = I like to ride. My horse is wooden. Everything turns!
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_carousel-klasse2 = The monkey sits on a wooden horse. It goes round and round while happy music plays.
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_carousel-klasse3 = The monkey loves it when everything spins. It has found a place where colourful wooden horses go round in a circle under a striped roof. A cheerful tune plays along. The monkey sits backwards on a horse and squeals with delight.

# loc_trampoline — ground-level trampoline in the lawn
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_trampoline-kiga = trampoline
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_trampoline-klasse1 = Boing, boing, boing! I jump up high. The ground is bouncy.
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_trampoline-klasse2 = The monkey bounces on a round blue mat in the grass. It is so springy that the monkey jumps almost up to the sky.
mission-monkey-riddle-loc_trampoline-klasse3 = Monkeys like to jump from branch to branch. Our monkey has found something even better: a round blue mat lying in the lawn. Every time it lands on it, the mat throws it back up into the air. It does somersaults and laughs.

# shown when the animal is back in its enclosure (mission complete, GAME-RESCUE §8)
mission-monkey-home = Great! The monkey is home again.

## 8. Giraffe — loc_lookout_tower, loc_train, loc_playground (level_2)

animal-giraffe = Giraffe
animal-giraffe-more = More about the giraffe

# Facts (never a place word, ANIM-007); kiga: one word next to a picture
mission-giraffe-facts-kiga = neck
mission-giraffe-facts-klasse1 = My neck is very long. I eat leaves. My tongue is blue.
mission-giraffe-facts-klasse2 = Giraffes are the tallest animals in the world. With their long neck they reach the highest leaves. Their tongue is dark blue and very long.
mission-giraffe-facts-klasse3 = Giraffes live in Africa and are the tallest animals in the world. Although their neck is so long, it has only seven bones, just like yours. Their tongue is almost as long as your arm and dark blue. Every giraffe has its own pattern of patches. Giraffes often sleep standing up, and only for a short time.

# loc_lookout_tower — wooden lookout tower with stairs and a high platform
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_lookout_tower-kiga = tower
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_lookout_tower-klasse1 = I am very tall. People stand up high. I look at them.
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_lookout_tower-klasse2 = The giraffe stands next to a tall wooden frame with stairs. Up on the platform it is right at eye level with the visitors.
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_lookout_tower-klasse3 = Visitors like to climb many steps to look out over the zoo from above. Today they get a surprise: a long neck pops up right next to the railing! The giraffe is so tall that it can look the people up there in the face. It hopes that somebody will give it a few leaves.

# loc_train — little zoo train (engine + 2 wagons) at its station
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_train-kiga = train
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_train-klasse1 = Toot, toot! Here is a station. The bell rings.
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_train-klasse2 = The giraffe stands by a little colourful engine with two wagons. It is much taller than the chimney.
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_train-klasse3 = The zoo has a little railway that visitors love to ride. Today it is standing still at the platform, and the giraffe has become curious. It sniffs the chimney of the engine and looks into the empty wagons. When it bumps the bell, it rings loudly.

# loc_playground — playground with slide and swings
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_playground-kiga = playground
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_playground-klasse1 = My neck is long. Children slide here. Children swing here.
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_playground-klasse2 = The giraffe stands where children slide and swing. It is much taller than the slide.
mission-giraffe-riddle-loc_playground-klasse3 = The giraffe is very curious. It heard children laughing and followed the sound. Now it stands between the swings and the slide. With its long tongue it pulls leaves off the trees.

# shown when the animal is back in its enclosure (mission complete, GAME-RESCUE §8)
mission-giraffe-home = Great! The giraffe is home again.

## 9. Lion — loc_sun_rocks, loc_stage, loc_deckchairs (level_2)

animal-lion = Lion
animal-lion-more = More about the lion

# Facts (never a place word, ANIM-007); kiga: one word next to a picture
mission-lion-facts-kiga = mane
mission-lion-facts-klasse1 = I have a mane. I roar very loudly. I sleep a lot.
mission-lion-facts-klasse2 = Lions live in Africa in a group called a pride. Only the males have a big mane. You can hear a lion's roar from very far away.
mission-lion-facts-klasse3 = Lions live in Africa and are the only big cats that live in groups. Such a group is called a pride. Only the males have a thick mane. Their roar is so loud that you can hear it far away. Lions spend most of the day sleeping comfortably.

# loc_sun_rocks — big flat rocks in full sun, no shade
mission-lion-riddle-loc_sun_rocks-kiga = rocks
mission-lion-riddle-loc_sun_rocks-klasse1 = I am lazy. The sun is warm. I lie on stone.
mission-lion-riddle-loc_sun_rocks-klasse2 = The lion lies lazily on big, warm stones in the sun. It yawns and almost falls asleep.
mission-lion-riddle-loc_sun_rocks-klasse3 = The lion is the king of animals, but today it is mostly lazy. It found the warmest spot in the zoo. There are big, flat stones there that the sun shines on all day. It stretches out and yawns loudly.

# loc_stage — round wooden music stage with a pointed roof, drums
mission-lion-riddle-loc_stage-kiga = stage
mission-lion-riddle-loc_stage-klasse1 = I like to roar loudly. Music plays here. There are drums here.
mission-lion-riddle-loc_stage-klasse2 = The lion lies in front of a round wooden platform with a pointed roof and drums on it. It roars as if it wants to sing.
mission-lion-riddle-loc_stage-klasse3 = The lion is the king of animals, and today it also wants to be the king of music. It has found a round wooden place with a pointed roof where musicians usually play. There are drums and a xylophone. The lion roars as loudly as it can, and it sounds almost like a song.

# loc_deckchairs — striped deckchairs under a big sunshade
mission-lion-riddle-loc_deckchairs-kiga = deckchair
mission-lion-riddle-loc_deckchairs-klasse1 = I am so sleepy. There is a sunshade here. The chairs are striped.
